    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q32-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why $2ab\\cos C<2ab$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "In a triangle, $0<C<\\pi$, so $\\cos C<1$. Since $2ab>0$, $2ab\\cos C<2ab$.",
          "worked": "In a triangle, $0<C<\\pi$, so $\\cos C<1$. Since $a,b>0$, multiplying by $2ab$ preserves the inequality:\n$$2ab\\cos C<2ab.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q32-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By using the cosine rule, show that $c<a+b$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p32-q32-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "c<a+b",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p32-q32-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cos C>-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " in the cosine rule to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "c^2<(a+b)^2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then take positive square roots.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Since $0<C<\\pi$, $\\cos C>-1$. With $a,b>0$, this gives $-2ab\\cos C<2ab$. By the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}c^2&=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C\\\\c^2&<a^2+b^2+2ab\\\\c^2&<(a+b)^2\\end{align*}$$\nTaking positive square roots gives $c<a+b$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
